  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_cc90fdef38f94ad6a97d4c806817f80f",
      "statement": "The composition root mounts non-grounded domains by `kind`: `workflow` goes through the helpdesk Agent Framework workflow mount, `tool` goes through builder or platform Agent Framework mounts, and `graph` goes through a LangGraph-specific mount. Because the LangGraph adapter does not accept FastAPI dependencies, the graph mount wraps it in an `APIRouter` and then includes that router with the normal domain dependencies so auth and entitlement still apply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/backend/app/registry.py#L182-L247",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55bba11a7aa6fa9bdb02048b328dee0d8d0b3e932bf5a64277f73e5fd977ef42:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/backend/app/registry.py#L250-L270",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e17f3d0570f8e4b1f3f7593b91ec88dbcda6a2aea5b274238c45e983ed2ed21b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b509f2eb20e54b1ba9d33b63629d62fa",
      "statement": "The frontend domain registry and console treat `helpdesk` as `workflow`, `platform` and `builder` as `tool`, and `oncall` plus `deepcall` as `graph`, and the console mounts `TicketApproval` for Agent Framework `workflow` and `tool` domains while mounting `GraphApproval` only for `graph` domains.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/frontend/components/console/AssuranceConsole.tsx#L150-L167",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:abf2c181d83b025bff4eb8980b2f7f89ee48dcb3f7ca5ec6865cfe3f0f5e953a:"
