    {
      "id": "claim_12ef46d0fb9940178a780cfa49a9f673",
      "statement": "The declarative helpdesk workflow test proves that a declared human step really becomes the same runtime gate shape: it builds the published helpdesk YAML into a `Workflow`, verifies that a minimal YAML `Question` step emits `request_info`, resumes it with `ExternalInputResponse`, and checks that later executors run, while nonexistent referenced agents fail at workflow construction time.",
      "evidence": [
